# Credentials for the DEV workbench service: where the OPERATOR supplies the
# key material. Nothing in this file is a value - copy it, fill it in, and keep
# the filled copy OUTSIDE the repositories (it is never committed).
#
# The credential that authenticates a PRIVATE git source is resolved through the
# credentials SERVICE, and the provider implementing it is a PLUGIN
# (`credentials-basic`, declared in config.yml). There is NO core provider and no
# "bootstrap" provider set: the core ships the credentials DEFINITION only. What
# makes this work is the GATE - sources that need NO credential are walked FIRST
# (that is where the provider plugin comes from) and a source carrying `auth:` is
# DEFERRED until such a plugin is registered, never fetched anonymously. Which
# providers may answer is `credentials.providers` in config.yml (absent = every
# declared provider, the dev default). See the core docs/CREDENTIALS.md.
#
# Two equivalent ways to supply the GitHub App PRIVATE KEY:
#
# 1. ENV var (the `env` provider; name looked up exactly, then ENV-normalised):
#      export GITHUB_APP_KEY="$(cat /path/to/app.private-key.pem)"
#    Multiline values are awkward in an env var, which is why the `file`
#    provider is listed too and is the recommended one for a PEM.
#
# 2. FILE (the `file` provider): a JSON/YAML MAPPING of credential name -> value
#    at the path configured in config.yml under `plugins.credentials-basic.file.path`
#    (default in this repository: /opt/workspace/workbench-secrets/credentials.yml).
#    /opt is mapped in-and-out by the compose service, so the same path is
#    visible inside and outside the container:
#
#      mkdir -p /opt/workspace/workbench-secrets
#      cat > /opt/workspace/workbench-secrets/credentials.yml <<'YAML'
#      GITHUB_APP_KEY: |
#        -----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----
#        ... app private key, not versioned, never committed ...
#        -----END PRIVATE KEY-----
#      YAML
#      chmod 600 /opt/workspace/workbench-secrets/credentials.yml
#
# The App must be INSTALLED on the private repository
# (nexuslbs/workbench-plugins-private) with at least `Contents: read`; the
# installation id and the app id are non-secret identifiers and live in
# config.yml.
#
# NO CREDENTIAL = NO BREAKAGE: when neither place supplies GITHUB_APP_KEY, the
# private source is reported as an error naming the source and the reason, and
# every other source still loads. The fetch is never retried anonymously.
